  "claim": "This work was influenced by the opera in four acts which is 2 more acts than Mitridate, re di Ponto. The Opéra-Comique performs this work.",
  "evidencia": "Page: La jolie fille de Perth. Sentence: La jolie fille de Perth \"(The Fair Maid of Perth)\" is an opera in four acts by Georges Bizet (1838–1875), from a libretto by Jules-Henri Vernoy de Saint-Georges and Jules Adenis, after the novel by Sir Walter Scott.\nPage: Mitridate, re di Ponto. Sentence: Mitridate, re di Ponto (\"Mithridates, King of Pontus\"), K. 87 (74a), is an early opera seria in three acts by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.\nPage: La dame blanche. Sentence: The opera's musical style also heavily influenced later operas like \"Lucia di Lammermoor\", \"I puritani\" and \"La jolie fille de Perth\".\nPage: Opéra-Comique. Sentence: Mainstays of the repertory at the Opéra-Comique during its history have included the following works which have each been performed more than 1,000 times by the company: \"Cavalleria Rusticana\", \"Le chalet\", \"La dame blanche\", \"Le domino noir\", \"La fille du régiment\", \"Lakmé\", \"Manon\", \"Mignon\", \"Les noces de Jeannette\", \"Le pré aux clercs\", \"Tosca\", \"La bohème\", \"Werther\" and \"Carmen\", the last having been performed more than 2,500 times.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: La jolie fille de Perth. Sentence: La jolie fille de Perth \"(The Fair Maid of Perth)\" is an opera in four acts by Georges Bizet (1838–1875), from a libretto by Jules-Henri Vernoy de Saint-Georges and Jules Adenis, after the novel by Sir Walter Scott.\nPage: Mitridate, re di Ponto. Sentence: Mitridate, re di Ponto (\"Mithridates, King of Pontus\"), K. 87 (74a), is an early opera seria in three acts by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.\nPage: La dame blanche. Sentence: The opera's musical style also heavily influenced later operas like \"Lucia di Lammermoor\", \"I puritani\" and \"La jolie fille de Perth\".\nPage: Opéra-Comique. Sentence: Mainstays of the repertory at the Opéra-Comique during its history have included the following works which have each been performed more than 1,000 times by the company: \"Cavalleria Rusticana\", \"Le chalet\", \"La dame blanche\", \"Le domino noir\", \"La fille du régiment\", \"Lakmé\", \"Manon\", \"Mignon\", \"Les noces de Jeannette\", \"Le pré aux clercs\", \"Tosca\", \"La bohème\", \"Werther\" and \"Carmen\", the last having been performed more than 2,500 times.",
